  "changes": [
    {
      "path": "/questions/6/view/options/1/text",
      "before": "$(q_n)$：前5项为 $10,\\ 20,\\ 30,\\ 40,\\ 50$；通项为 $q_n=10n$。",
      "after": "$(q_n)$：前5项为 $10,\\ 20,\\ 30,\\ 40,\\ 50$；通项为 $q_n=10^n$。"
    },
    {
      "path": "/questions/6/view/options/5/text",
      "before": "$(p_n)$：前5项为 $20,\\ 30,\\ 40,\\ 50,\\ 60$；通项为 $p_n=10(n+1)$。",
      "after": "$(p_n)$：前5项为 $10,\\ 20,\\ 30,\\ 40,\\ 50$；通项为 $p_n=10(n+1)$。"
    },
    {
      "path": "/questions/6/intent/unit_reason",
      "before": "Each response is a complete prefix-plus-formula pair. Multiple selection compares all four initial-value rules in one coherent task; matching only an early coincidence, particularly 2,4, does not settle a formula.",
      "after": "Each alternative is a complete prefix-plus-formula pair across the four initial-value rules. Option f has the correct prefix and an incorrect formula, while b has an incorrect prefix and the correct formula. The complete correct set therefore requires judging both components: checking prefixes alone adds f; checking formulas alone adds b. Multiple selection retains one coherent comparison, not per-term or per-slot questions."
    },
    {
      "path": "/questions/6/key/rationales/1/derivation",
      "before": "Replace q_(n+1)=10q_n by q_(n+1)=q_n+10. Starting at 10 gives the displayed arithmetic prefix and q_n=10+10(n-1)=10n.",
      "after": "The general formula q_n=10^n is correctly obtained from the supplied initial factor 10 and n-1 multiplications. The prefix is incorrectly generated by repeatedly adding 10, producing 10,20,30,40,50 instead of the geometric prefix. Its formula alone is true but the required combined claim is false."
    },
    {
      "path": "/questions/6/key/rationales/1/misconception",
      "before": "Treat multiplying by 10 as adding 10 when extending the sequence and deriving its formula.",
      "after": "Remember the correct geometric general term but extend the early terms using addition instead of multiplication."
    },
    {
      "path": "/questions/6/key/rationales/5/derivation",
      "before": "Count an increment even at the first position: p_n=10+10n=10(n+1), giving 20,30,40,50,60 at indices 1 through 5.",
      "after": "The displayed prefix is correctly obtained by four successive additions of 10 after p_1=10. The proposed general formula incorrectly counts n additions rather than n-1, giving 10+10n=10(n+1); it fails p_1=10. Its prefix alone is true but the required combined claim is false."
    },
    {
      "path": "/questions/6/key/rationales/5/misconception",
      "before": "Apply n increments after the supplied first value instead of n-1, shifting both prefix and formula.",
      "after": "Correctly iterate the recurrence for early terms, then apply an extra increment when translating the index into a general formula."
    }
  ],
